{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"3a2192de","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.004064,"end_time":"2026-10-08T07:34:49.65466+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-08T07:34:49.650596+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# 02_LIN-SVM_TF-IDF\n","\n","**Role.** Classical baseline. Calibrated linear SVM over word-level TF-IDF features.\n","\n","**Research questions.** RQ1 as a classical baseline. RQ2 and RQ3 as a second linear model over the same word features as notebook 01, which shows whether reliance depends on the loss (hinge against logistic) when the features are held fixed. RQ4 through its probability artifact.\n","\n","**Kaggle inputs.**\n","1. This repository as an input dataset (provides `tools/notebook_kit.py` and the committed split mirror).\n","2. The output of `00_create_dataset_and_splits` (the `research_foundation/` folder).\n","\n","**Accelerator.** CPU.\n","\n","**Outputs.**\n","- `results_summary/02_LIN-SVM_TF-IDF/` and `research_loop/probs/02_LIN-SVM_TF-IDF__*`: text-free, copied into the repository.\n","- `external/02_LIN-SVM_TF-IDF/`: weights, per-post predictions and per-post attributions. Uploaded to a Kaggle Dataset and recorded in the run manifest; never committed.\n","\n","**Protocol.** Configurations and the decision threshold are selected on the validation split. The test split is evaluated once, in section 8. Every attribution comes from one method, SHAP's partition explainer over a word-level text masker, so techniques are comparable.\n","\n","**What this notebook never shows.** Cell outputs are committed, so no cell prints, displays or plots a post, a row id or a text hash. Outputs are counts, metrics, configurations and word-level tables.\n","\n","**Responsible use.** A research artifact for studying what classifiers of extremist content rely on. Labels are post-level and features are text only; nothing here supports decisions about people, accounts or communities."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"4f0418a6"