,"metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.003563,"end_time":"2026-10-08T07:35:09.396812+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-08T07:35:09.393249+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 4. Features and model\n","\n","The model is one scikit-learn pipeline: a word-level TF-IDF vectorizer, followed by a linear SVM whose margins are calibrated to probabilities. `predict_proba_texts` maps raw strings to P(EXTREMIST) through that pipeline. It is the single entry point used for the validation threshold, the test evaluation and every explainer run, so the model that is explained is exactly the calibrated model that predicts."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"id":"b9b24e3d","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-08T07:35:09.405424Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-08T07:35:09.405106Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-08T07:35:09.412845Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-08T07:35:09.412223Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.013998,"end_time":"2026-10-08T07:35:09.414372+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-08T07:35:09.400374+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def expand_grid(grid):\n","    \"\"\"Every combination of the grid's values, as a list of dicts.\"\"\"\n","    keys = list(grid)\n","    return [dict(zip(keys, combo)) for combo in product(*(grid[key] for key in keys))]\n","\n","\n","def build_features(hyperparameters):\n","    \"\"\"An unfitted word-level TF-IDF vectorizer for one configuration.\"\"\"\n","    return TfidfVectorizer(\n","        max_features=hyperparameters[\"max_features\"],\n","        ngram_range=tuple(hyperparameters[\"ngram_range\"]),\n","        min_df=hyperparameters[\"min_df\"],\n","        max_df=hyperparameters[\"max_df\"],\n","        sublinear_tf=hyperparameters[\"sublinear_tf\"],\n","        lowercase=True,\n","        strip_accents=None,\n","        dtype=np.float32,\n","    )\n","\n","\n","def build_pipeline(hyperparameters):\n","    \"\"\"An unfitted features + calibrated linear SVM pipeline for one configuration.\"\"\"\n","    base_model = LinearSVC(\n","        C=hyperparameters[\"C\"],\n","        class_weight=hyperparameters[\"class_weight\"],\n","        max_iter=CONFIG[\"model\"][\"max_iter\"],\n","        tol=CONFIG[\"model\"][\"tol\"],\n","        random_state=CONFIG[\"random_seed\"],\n","    )\n","    classifier = CalibratedClassifierCV(\n","        estimator=base_model,\n","        method=CONFIG[\"calibration\"][\"method\"],\n","        cv=CONFIG[\"calibration\"][\"cv\"],\n","    )\n","    return Pipeline([(\"features\", build_features(hyperparameters)), (\"classifier\", classifier)])\n","\n","\n","pipeline = None  # fitted in section 6\n","\n","\n","def predict_proba_texts(texts):\n","    \"\"\"P(EXTREMIST) for a list of raw strings, through the fitted pipeline.\"\"\"\n","    return pipeline.predict_proba(list(texts))[:, 1]"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"301218b7","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.003655,"end_time":"2026-10-08T07:35:09.421234+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-08T07:35:09.417579+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 5. Ablation on validation\n","\n","Fit every configuration of the grid on the training split and score it on validation at the screening threshold. The configuration with the highest validation accuracy is selected; ties break on validation ROC-AUC, then on configuration id. The test split is not touched."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":5,"id":"bc4b1f4c","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-08T07:35:09.43051Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-08T07:35:09.430131Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-08T07:35:31.992676Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-08T07:35:31.991946Z"},"papermill":{"duration":22.570397,"end_time":"2026-10-08T07:35:31.996172+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-08T07:35:09.425775+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Configurations compared on validatio